  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_023, multimodal/multiprofile/transformer/weighted, acc=0.713) outperforms rna_only/multiprofile/avgpool (config_041, acc=0.650), but this gap conflates two changes: adding the image modality AND switching from avgpool to transformer aggregation. We know weighted fusion > concat at the avgpool level (0.678 vs 0.632), and transformer > avgpool at the weighted level (0.713 vs 0.678), but we have no data on whether transformer aggregation alone (without image) can close most of that gap. Question: config_001 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) is a clean single-variable ablation of config_023—removing only the image modality while keeping the best aggregation and profile settings. This directly isolates the marginal contribution of the image modality at the transformer aggregation level. Why best use of budget: If rna_only+transformer approaches 0.713, the image modality is not adding meaningful value and further multimodal experiments are low-value; if it stays near 0.65–0.67, the image modality is genuinely contributing and we should exploit multimodal directions (e.g., better image encoders or fusion). This single experiment resolves a fundamental design uncertainty that will determine the entire remaining search strategy, making it the highest-information next step."
}

